{"content":[{"c":["ELISHAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Javan’s son (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.4","r":"Gen.10.4","rawR":"Gen.10.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.4","value":"Gen.10.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.7","r":"1Chr.1.7","rawR":"1Chr.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.7","value":"1Chr.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:7"},"). The Hebrew term for Greece is Javan; hence, Elishah could be the term for the western Aegean islands or coastlands (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.5","r":"Gen.10.5","rawR":"Gen.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.5","value":"Gen.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:5"},") that supplied dye stuffs to the inhabitants of Tyre (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.7","r":"Ezek.27.7","rawR":"Ezek.27.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.7","value":"Ezek.27.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:7"},"). The Jewish historian Josephus identified Elishah with the Aeolians; other suggestions are Carthage in North Africa, Hellas, Italy, and Elis. A Mediterranean site seems probable from the context of ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.6-7","r":"Ezek.27.6-7","rawR":"Ezek.27.6-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.6-7","value":"Ezek.27.6-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezekiel 27:6-7"},", perhaps an area of Cyprus that exported copper."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elishah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.4","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.4","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.4"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.7"},{"anchorText":"Gn 10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.5"},{"anchorText":"Ez 27:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.7","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.7","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.7"},{"anchorText":"Ezekiel 27:6-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.6-7","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.6-7","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.6-7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"773002dc6d5fd1b4275c4645e69e0fbda05c0c5f4bc39b1b82019d8143a62cbd","sourceItemName":"Elishah","sourceItemOrder":114,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elishah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elishah","title":"Elishah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}